    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "A bag contains $p$ marbles.\n(a) What does $p$ represent?\n(b) The bag contains $14$ marbles. What is the value of $p$?",
        "solution_text": "(a) The pronumeral $p$ represents the number of marbles in the bag.\n(b) The number of marbles is $14$, so $p=14$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For each pronumeral, state whether it is a variable. Explain.\n(a) $r$ is the number of pages Mia reads in a week. This can change each week.\n(b) $s$ is the number of sides of a pentagon.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $r$ can represent many different numbers, so it is a variable.\n(b) Every pentagon has $5$ sides, so $s=5$ is fixed. It is a pronumeral, but it is not a variable in this context."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "In $a+a+b$, the first $a$ represents $9$.\n(a) What does the second $a$ represent?\n(b) Must $b$ represent a number different from $9$? Explain.",
        "solution_text": "(a) The same pronumeral has the same value in one expression. The second $a$ also represents $9$.\n(b) No. Different pronumerals may represent different numbers, but they do not have to. For example, $b$ could represent $4$ or $9$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Complete the statements.\n(a) Pronumerals, such as $k$ and $t$, are letters or symbols that represent .......... .\n(b) A pronumeral with many possible numerical values is called a .......... .\n(c) Algebra uses .......... to represent numbers and communicate mathematical relationships.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Numbers. Each letter stands for a number.\n(b) Variable. A variable can represent many different numbers.\n(c) Pronumerals. These symbols represent numbers in mathematical relationships."
      }
    ],
